landing-review: landing 11-4c (the fps, scaffold, GAF and posebake GL halves), level medium, 2026-09-19

Range main...HEAD at c62270a..b542817, main at c62270a; a dedicated read-only
reviewer with the pristine build and objdump, xhigh effort, 59 tool uses.
NO HIGH findings and no correctness defect. Two MEDIUM, four LOW. All six
verified against the code before acting.

The reviewer re-derived the landing's whole premise from the bottom up rather
than taking it: tagpu_vk_owns_present() is s_ownWin != 0, set once from
render_vk.c:145 before the frame loop; render_ogl.c no longer exists; dd.c
assigns only gdi_render_main and vk_render_main; render_gdi.c makes zero
tagpu_ calls; tagpu_overlay_draw has one live call site. It also proved both
pragma brackets with a planted unused static rather than reading them, and
recorded that -fsyntax-only does not surface -Wunused-variable, so the probe
needs a real compile.

M1 -- THE FINDING THAT EARNS THE REVIEW. 11-4c deleted tagpu_fps.c's s_state
because nothing could raise it once the bring-up went, and in the same landing
left tagpu_scaffold.c's s_state, plus s_texW/s_texH, write-only in exactly the
same way -- with two comments still presenting s_state as live, one inside
tagpu_scaffold_frameinfo, the function the 4b-1 review had already fixed once
for testing it. Confirmed by grep: assigned at :80 and :510, read nowhere.
All three deleted; both comments rewritten to say there is no state left to
ask. Fixed in 4ba9ad2.

M2 -- the 64 cross-build pairs were taken on a fixture that leaves
`scaf=0 fps=0`, so the two passes this landing changed most contributed no
pixels to the only pixel-exact measurement; the armed run was eyeballed. The
reviewer offered the closure and it holds: every construct removed from
tagpu_scaffold_frame is inside `if (gl_draws)`, or is
`if (gl_draws && s_state == 2) return;`, or is the gl_draws declaration, and
gl_draws is 0 by the ordering -- so the transformation is EXACT, not nearly
so. Verified independently by extracting tagpu_scaffold_overlay,
tagpu_scaffold_frameinfo, stamp_gaf and stamp_px from both revisions with a
masked brace matcher: identical hashes. unit=0 therefore reproduces before
the landing. Both notes now say so, and say what the 64 pairs did not cover.

L1 -- tagpu_posebake.c's last three GL calls guarded vao/vbo whose only writer
was the deleted bring-up: permanently false, unreachable. Removed; glreset
reduced to the generation bump; opengl_utils.h dropped with them. The FIELDS
stay because tagpu_posedraw.c still reads m->vao -- and its own guard
`if (!tagpu_vk_owns_present() && !m->vao) return NULL;` now has BOTH terms
dead, which is 11-5's to take.

L2 -- tagpu_text_tex() lost its last caller when 11-4c removed tagpu_fps.c's
glBindTexture. Nothing was lost with it (the Vulkan-facing counter is s_agen,
bumped by the atlas writer). Already scoped to 11-5; recorded there.

L3 -- the finding with the real downside, and it is about prose: deleting the
GL half orphaned the comments that explain why the CPU mirror memcpy is not a
redundant second copy. Read today they assert a property of nothing, which
makes the only copy of the art look like dead weight to remove. Each rewritten
to state what the mirror IS and to say that deleting it deletes the sprite.

L4 -- `GLuint t = 0; ... a->tex = t;` was a constant dressed as a texture that
might have been created. Now `a->tex = 0`.

Three -Wmisleading-indentation warnings the reviewer surfaced are PRE-EXISTING:
byte-identical at main (tagpu_scaffold.c's at :446 before the landing deleted
129 lines above them), and each is two complete one-line ifs. Not acted on.

RE-VERIFICATION after the fixes was by OBJECT IDENTITY rather than another
A/B, because it is exhaustive where an A/B samples: tagpu_scaffold.o,
tagpu_gaf.o and tagpu_fps.o compile byte-identical across the fix commit;
